{
  "tofu": "VERSION",
  "verb": "docs",
  "ok": true,
  "at": "AT",
  "data": {
    "topic": "settings",
    "title": "Settings",
    "summary": "every setting, its default, what it takes, and how to change it",
    "markdown": "## What it is\n\nA setting is a named switch, like `theme` or `gatePrompt`. Each one has a\ndefault, and you only write the ones you want different.\n\nThe settings come in groups:\n\n- Appearance: theme, density, animations, statusBar, colorMode\n- Interaction: composer, gatePrompt, readBeforeEdit\n- Context: compaction, chatShowsTools, agentFeeds, showThinking, thinkingSummary, images, projectInstructionsCap, instructionSources, skills\n- Files: diffContext, hyperlinks, groupByAgent\n- Shell: persistentRegistry, logTail, killConfirm, shell, foldHidesShell\n- Turn: decisionCap, turnMaySpawn, subAgentsPerTurn, subAgentDepth, agentSources, modelTier.genius, modelTier.smart, modelTier.worker, modelTier.dumb\n- Browser: browser, browserDriver, browserSteps\n\n## Where it lives\n\n- `~/.tofu/settings.json`: yours, in every project\n- `.tofu/settings.json` in a project: that project only\n\nThe project file wins over yours, and yours wins over the default.\n\n## Change it\n\n    tofu settings set <key> <value>\n\nwrites your file. Add `--scope project` to write the project's instead:\n\n    tofu settings set --scope project gatePrompt ask\n\nA true or false setting takes `true` or `false`. A list takes commas and no\nspaces, like `tofu,claude`. A value the setting does not take is refused and\nnothing is written. An older value a setting used to take, like\n`AGENTS.md,CLAUDE.md` for `instructionSources`, is read and written as the\nchoice it became. In the app, type `/settings` for the same list\nwith a search.\n\nA setting marked (on the next start) is read once when tofu opens, so quit\nand open it again.\n\n## Check it\n\n    tofu settings\n\nprints every setting by group, its value, and `project`, `global` or\n`default` for where it came from, with `●` on the ones you set.\n\n    tofu settings get <key>\n\nprints one value. Both take `--json` and print one JSON document. `set`\nprints one `~` line with the file and `→ undo:` with the command that puts\nthe old value back.\n\n## Undo it\n\nSet it back to the default shown below, or delete its line from the\nsettings file. With the line gone, the next file down wins.\n\n## Every setting\n",
    "settings": [
      {
        "key": "theme",
        "category": "Appearance",
        "default": "tofu",
        "takes": "one of tofu, tofu light, tofu dusk, Solarized Light, Dracula, Nord, Gruvbox, terminal",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "tofu uses Zed Nu Disco; choose a palette"
      },
      {
        "key": "density",
        "category": "Appearance",
        "default": "comfortable",
        "takes": "one of compact, comfortable, spacious",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "Spacing across lists and panels"
      },
      {
        "key": "animations",
        "category": "Appearance",
        "default": "subtle",
        "takes": "one of off, subtle, full",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "Motion for conversational states"
      },
      {
        "key": "statusBar",
        "category": "Appearance",
        "default": "compact",
        "takes": "one of compact, detailed, hidden",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "Context, quotas, and runtime counters"
      },
      {
        "key": "colorMode",
        "category": "Appearance",
        "default": "auto",
        "takes": "one of auto, truecolor, 256 colors, ANSI 16",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "Terminal color capability"
      },
      {
        "key": "composer",
        "category": "Interaction",
        "default": "standard",
        "takes": "one of standard, compact, expanded",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "Enter sends; Shift+Enter inserts a line break"
      },
      {
        "key": "gatePrompt",
        "category": "Interaction",
        "default": "run",
        "takes": "one of run, ask",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "run lets a gated call go, ask waits for you; a rule's shadow or enforced is a different switch"
      },
      {
        "key": "readBeforeEdit",
        "category": "Interaction",
        "default": "true",
        "takes": "true or false",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "an edit or a write to a file this session has not read, or that changed since it was read, is refused"
      },
      {
        "key": "compaction",
        "category": "Context",
        "default": "adaptive",
        "takes": "one of adaptive, manual, off",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "Automatic transcript compaction; not built yet, so no choice changes a turn"
      },
      {
        "key": "chatShowsTools",
        "category": "Context",
        "default": "false",
        "takes": "true or false",
        "restart": false,
        "description": "chat shows every tool call"
